```python
import os

def log_files(directory):
    for entry in os.listdir(directory):
        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(directory, entry)):
            print(entry)

log_files('/path/to/directory')
```

This prints each filename. If you want it to recurse into subdirectories, I can swap `os.listdir` for `os.walk`.
